      "name": "Format Quote"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Analyze this real-time quote and decide: BUY, SELL, or HOLD.\n\nSymbol:     {{ $json.body.symbol }}\nBid:        {{ $json.body.bp }}\nAsk:        {{ $json.body.ap }}\nBid Size:   {{ $json.body.bs }}\nAsk Size:   {{ $json.body.as }}\nLast Price: {{ $json.body.lp }}\nSpread:     {{ ($json.body.ap - $json.body.bp).toFixed(4) }}\nBid/Ask Ratio: {{ ($json.body.bs / $json.body.as).toFixed(2) }}\nTime (UTC): {{ $json.body.timestamp }}\n\nSignal hints:\n- Spread > 0.05 = avoid (too wide for scalp)\n- Bid size > Ask size = buying pressure → lean BUY\n- Ask size > Bid size = selling pressure → lean SELL\n- Use Last Price as your entry_price base\n\nReturn ONLY the JSON object. No explanation. No markdown.",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "=You are a professional scalp trading AI executing real paper trades via Alpaca Markets.\n\nSTRICT RULES:\n- US market hours ONLY: 9:30 AM – 4:00 PM ET. If outside hours, return action \"hold\".\n- Max 10 shares per trade.\n- Scalp logic only: tight stops, quick targets, small spreads.\n- Avoid HOLD unless no clear direction or outside market hours.\n- If signal is slightly bullish/bearish, still allow trade with lower confidence.\n- You MUST return ONLY a raw JSON object. No markdown, no explanation, no preamble, no trailing commas.\n- All JSON keys must be in double quotes.\n- Numbers must be plain floats, not strings.\n\nPRICE LOGIC ENFORCEMENT (non-negotiable):\n- BUY:  stop_loss < entry_price < take_profit\n- SELL: take_profit < entry_price < stop_loss\n- HOLD: set entry_price = last_price, stop_loss = 0, take_profit = 0, qty = 0\n\nCONFIDENCE RULES:\n- Only act (BUY/SELL) if confidence >= 0.55\n- If confidence < 0.55, return action = \"hold\"\n\nSCALP SIZING RULES:\n- stop_loss must be within 0.3% of entry_price\n- take_profit must be at least 2x the stop distance (1:2 risk/reward minimum)\n- qty must be between 1 and 5 (integer only)\n\nOUTPUT SCHEMA — return exactly these fields, nothing else:\n{\n  \"action\": \"buy\" | \"sell\" | \"hold\",\n  \"symbol\": \"<ticker from input>\",\n  \"confidence\": <0.0 – 1.0>,\n  \"qty\": <integer 1–5>,\n  \"entry_price\": <float>,\n  \"stop_loss\": <float>,\n  \"take_profit\": <float>,\n  \"reason\": \"<max 12 words, describe signal>\"\n}"
        }
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 3.1,
      "position": [
        1008,
        720
      ],
      "id": "8eb30c06-37b6-42cc-b258-0b574bec122e",
      "name": "Gemini Scalp Analyst"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const workflowStaticData = $getWorkflowStaticData('global');\nconst current = $input.first().json.output;\n\nconst lastAction   = workflowStaticData.lastAction   || '';\nconst lastSymbol   = workflowStaticData.lastSymbol   || '';\nconst lastActioned = workflowStaticData.lastActioned || 0;\n\nconst now          = Date.now();\nconst cooldownMs   = 5 * 60 * 1000; // 5 minute cooldown per symbol\nconst timeSinceLast = now - lastActioned;\n\n// Block if same action+symbol within cooldown window\nif (\n  current.action === lastAction &&\n  current.symbol === lastSymbol &&\n  timeSinceLast < cooldownMs\n) {\n  // Return empty — stops the flow here\n  return [];\n}\n\n// Save new state\nworkflowStaticData.lastAction   = current.action;\nworkflowStaticData.lastSymbol   = current.symbol;\nworkflowStaticData.lastActioned = now;\n\nreturn [{ json: $input.first().json }];"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1680,
        704
      ],
      "id": "b2b2fa88-af5c-4635-8dad-84fbc2915bad",
      "name": "Cooldown Filter"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const d = $input.first().json;\n\nconst entry = parseFloat(d.body?.ap); // always use ASK for BUY\nconst stop   = parseFloat(d.output?.stop_loss);\nconst tp     = parseFloat(d.output?.take_profit);\nconst qty    = parseInt(d.output?.qty);\nconst symbol = d.output?.symbol || d.symbol;\n\n// BUY bracket rules:\n// stop_loss MUST be below entry\n// take_profit MUST be above entry\nconst fixedStop = stop < entry \n  ? parseFloat(stop.toFixed(2)) \n  : parseFloat((entry * 0.998).toFixed(2));\n\nconst fixedTp = tp > entry \n  ? parseFloat(tp.toFixed(2)) \n  : parseFloat((entry * 1.004).toFixed(2));\n\n// Ensure minimum $0.10 gap\nconst finalTp = (fixedTp - fixedStop) < 0.10\n  ? parseFloat((fixedStop + 0.10).toFixed(2))\n  : fixedTp;\n\n// Risk/reward metrics\nconst stopDistance   = parseFloat((entry - fixedStop).toFixed(2));\nconst rewardDistance = parseFloat((finalTp - entry).toFixed(2));\nconst riskRewardRatio = parseFloat((rewardDistance / stopDistance).toFixed(2));\nconst maxRisk        = parseFloat((stopDistance * qty).toFixed(2));\nconst maxReward      = parseFloat((rewardDistance * qty).toFixed(2));\n\nreturn [{ json: {\n  // Order fields (used by Place BUY Order node)\n  symbol:           symbol,\n  qty:              qty,\n  entry_price:      parseFloat(entry.toFixed(2)),\n  stop_loss:        fixedStop,\n  take_profit:      finalTp,\n\n  // AI decision fields (for logging)\n  action:           d.output?.action      ?? 'buy',\n  confidence:       d.output?.confidence  ?? null,\n  reason:           d.output?.reason      ?? '',\n\n  // Risk metrics (for analysis)\n  stop_distance:    stopDistance,\n  reward_distance:  rewardDistance,\n  risk_reward:      riskRewardRatio,\n  max_risk_usd:     maxRisk,\n  max_reward_usd:   maxReward,\n\n  // Quote data at time of signal (for analysis)\n  bid:              d.body?.bp ?? null,\n  ask:              d.body?.ap ?? null,\n  bid_size:         d.body?.bs ?? null,\n  ask_size:         d.body?.as ?? null,\n  spread:           d.body?.ap && d.body?.bp \n                      ? parseFloat((d.body.ap - d.body.bp).toFixed(4)) \n                      : null,\n\n  // Timestamp\n  signal_time:      d.body?.timestamp ?? new Date().toISOString()\n}}];"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
